   167	def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:
   168	    """
   169	    Settle all ring transfers across the color-pointer square network and redraw each square at its net side length.
   170	
   171	    Input structure:
   172	    - The grid has one dominant background color.
   173	    - Each foreground object is a separated solid odd-sided square with a unique body color.
   174	    - Some squares have their center cell recolored to another square's body color; the rest stay pure.
   175	
   176	    Rule:
   177	    - Treat each recolored center as a pointer from that square to the square whose body color matches the marker.
   178	    - A pointing square loses one ring of thickness 1, so its side length decreases by 2.
   179	    - Every time a square is pointed to, it gains one ring, so its side length increases by 2 per incoming pointer.
